              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-steel-600">Cold press models (HN426, HN480) operate at higher system pressure (70 Mpa) and cake pressure (42-48 Mpa/cm²), allowing them to extract oil without heating the seeds. This preserves natural nutrients, flavor, and color — resulting in premium-grade oil that commands higher prices. Standard models use lower pressure and may require pre-heating seeds for optimal yield.</p>
          </details>
